<title>BELGIUM: Commission to settle 1992 farm fraud cases.</title>
<headline>Commission to settle 1992 farm fraud cases.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission is expected to announce on Wednesday that it has reached agreement with member states on most of the outstanding 209 million Ecus fines for farm fraud in 1992, officials said.</p>
<p>Agreement on the fines, involving Greece, Italy, Germany, Spain and France, was reached after discussions in an independent conciliation committee.</p>
<p>The penalties are expected to be reduced to around 67 million Ecus, of which two-thirds would be imposed on Greece for cotton and tobacco irregularities.</p>
<p>In March, the Commission fined 11 member states 787 million Ecus for misusing farm funds in 1992. the fines included 372 million Ecus for beef fraud, mostly in Ireland.</p>
</text>
